contentText:
ERNEST is opening up after leaving his opening slot on Ella Langley&#8217;s The Dandelion Tour in August.

In a post on Instagram on Monday (Sept. 7), ERNEST, 34, offered up thanks to his fans for their constant support and shared an update. &#8220;Bottom line is I was LOST&#8230; i recon I still am &#8230; but the search is on &#8230;. And that&#8217;s new to me,&#8221; he captioned his carousel post. &#8220;if anything, through this time, I am really starting to touch back in with my relationship with God… growing up in the church / Christian school, I would say I got a bit burnt out on it all.&#8221;

The post included video of a rainbow stretching over the wilderness, as well as photos of wildflowers, deer and turkeys, as well as a shot of ERNEST sitting on a chair on a deck and puffing on a cigarette.

He added, have spent far too long relying on my own (dumbass) way and thinking I can outsmart my better judgement…. That’s not the case…. I don’t have many answers at all…. But I do know where it’s starting…. A dialogue with something greater than ME. I can’t define it and don’t know if anyone really can… I just know that I have a beautiful life, family and friends that deserve me at my best. I deserve that for me too…. I’m not preaching by any means…. But I just wanted to let yall know I’m taking this time to dig and discover.&#8221;

He also offered up reassurances to fans, writing, &#8220;I love yall… and I love country music… Il be back to both soon!&#8221;

ERNEST &#8212; who boasts four songs on the Billboard Hot 100 so far &#8212; revealed on his Instagram Stories Aug. 28 that he would no longer be part of Langley&#8217;s tour, writing that it had taken a toll on his mental and physical health. &#8220;Hey y’all. The road has been dragging me down in a bad way. From mental to physical health,&#8221; he wrote at the time, saying he had planned to only be off the road for a few weeks in order to focus on &#8220;myself and my priorities.&#8221;

“I want to thank Ella for having me out on tour and wishing her the BEST in Auburn tonight and the rest of the tour,&#8221; he wrote at the time. &#8220;I look forward to coming back better and stronger. I owe it to myself and those affected by my actions. That starts now. Love y’all.&#8221;

In addition to previously holding down an opening slot on Langley&#8217;s The Dandelion Tour, ERNEST is also a cowriter on Langley&#8217;s song &#8220;Loving Life Again,&#8221; from her album Dandelion . He&#8217;s also a cowriter on Langley&#8217;s recently Koe Wetzel collab &#8220;Jaded.&#8221;
